  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0101_8474dad2baab.jpeg\" /><br />Let&rsquo;s first find points of intersection of two curves.<br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math> <math><mo>(</mo></math> neglect <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math> )<br />Hence point of intersections are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br />Tangent to the parabola at first quadrant point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8901;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> clearly point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfy the given equation of tangent."
  }
